Kvasir patch: compiler-rt builtins/int_lib.h
Why:       on a soft-float core (COMPILER_RT_ARMHF_TARGET not defined: the M0+) every COMPILER_RT_ABI builtin
           gets __attribute__((__used__)). The builtins are compiled into the image's LTO; calls to
           them appear only in code generation, after LTO has dropped what nothing referenced.
Upstream:  none - Kvasir links compiler-rt as bitcode into each image's LTO; upstream builds it native.
Proof:     not proven yet: build an M0+ image without it
Drop when: compiler-rt is linked as native objects instead of bitcode.

--- a/builtins/int_lib.h
+++ b/builtins/int_lib.h
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 #ifdef COMPILER_RT_ARMHF_TARGET
 #define COMPILER_RT_ABI
 #else
-#define COMPILER_RT_ABI __attribute__((__pcs__("aapcs")))
+#define COMPILER_RT_ABI __attribute__((__used__)) __attribute__((__pcs__("aapcs")))
 #endif
 #else
 #define COMPILER_RT_ABI
